    "description": "A big crocodile-line predator about 5 to 6 metres long from the Late Triassic of southern Poland, about 205 million years ago, named after the dragon of Kraków legend. It had a huge, deep skull, strong upright legs and two rows of bony scutes down its back. Its fossil droppings are full of crushed bone, so it bit through and swallowed the skeletons of its prey, a habit otherwise known only from tyrannosaurs."
