    "description": "One of the largest land predators of the Early and Middle Triassic, about 245 million years ago in southern Africa, reaching about 5 metres long. Its enormous head made up about a fifth of its length, with long jaws full of big curved teeth, on a bulky body with sturdy half-sprawling legs. One of the first giant archosaur relatives after the end-Permian extinction, it could overpower large plant-eating synapsids, but it was slow and heavy."
